---
import PathwayLandingLayout from '../../layouts/PathwayLandingLayout.astro';
import { getPathwayHero } from '@/lib/pathwayHeroes';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '@/lib/seo/config';
import { TEA_INVESTMENT_THRESHOLD } from '@/lib/eb5-investment';

const title = 'EB-5 Visa for Vietnamese Investors | StudentEB5';
const metaDescription =
  'EB-5 for Vietnamese investors covers investment basics, student timing, family funding, and source-of-funds considerations for Vietnamese nationals evaluating the program.';
const canonicalUrl = `${SITE_CONFIG.url}/pathways/eb5-for-vietnamese-investors`;
const h1 = 'EB-5 Visa for Vietnamese Investors';
const subhead =
  'A single overview for Vietnamese nationals (investors, students, and families) evaluating EB-5 as a path to permanent residence.';

const teaFormatted = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {
  style: 'currency',
  currency: 'USD',
  maximumFractionDigits: 0,
}).format(TEA_INVESTMENT_THRESHOLD);

const relatedResearch = [
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Cryptocurrency Source of Funds',
    url: '/research/eb5-cryptocurrency-source-of-funds',
    description: 'Documenting crypto origin, liquidation, and path of funds for EB-5 petitions.',
  },
  {
    title: 'EB-5 Immigrant Investor Program: Complete Guide',
    url: '/research/complete-2027-eb5-guide',
    description: 'Filing steps, rural set-asides, and current program structure overview.',
  },
];
const hero = getPathwayHero('eb5-for-vietnamese-investors');

---

<PathwayLandingLayout
  title={title}
  metaDescription={metaDescription}
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
  h1={h1}
  subhead={subhead}
  heroImage={hero.image}
  heroImageWebp={hero.webp}
  heroImageAlt="EB-5 pathway for Vietnamese investors"
  relatedResearch={relatedResearch}
  secondaryCtaText="Talk to Someone About EB-5 for Vietnamese Nationals"
  breadcrumbTitle="EB-5 for Vietnamese Investors"
  keywords={[
    'EB-5 for Vietnamese investors',
    'EB-5 Vietnam',
    'Vietnamese nationals EB-5',
    'EB-5 visa Vietnam',
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="extraCompliance">
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed border border-border rounded-lg bg-secondary/40 p-4 m-0">
      EB-5 investment involves financial risk, including potential loss of principal, and does not guarantee a green
      card, visa availability, or any specific processing time. Consult a qualified immigration attorney and a
      FINRA-registered financial adviser for guidance specific to your situation.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <p>
    The EB-5 Immigrant Investor Program offers eligible foreign nationals a path to a U.S. green card through a
    qualifying investment. Vietnamese nationals (whether investing from abroad, studying in the U.S. on F-1 status, or
    considering family-funded capital) evaluate the same core requirements: a qualifying investment, lawful
    source-of-funds documentation, project selection, and Form I-526E. Chargeability follows country of birth; confirm
    current category availability on the
    <a
      href="https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/legal/visa-law0/visa-bulletin.html"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">Visa Bulletin</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>For investors</h2>
  <p>
    Most investors use the reduced Targeted Employment Area (TEA) investment threshold of {teaFormatted}. That amount
    is capital only and excludes fees and professional costs. Source-of-funds documentation is especially important when
    capital has moved through multiple accounts, businesses, or (for some investors) cryptocurrency paths that later
    convert to fiat. See
    <a href="/research/eb5-cryptocurrency-source-of-funds">EB-5 cryptocurrency source of funds</a> when crypto is part
    of the history, and the
    <a href="/research/complete-2027-eb5-guide">complete EB-5 guide</a> for program structure. Process steps live on
    <a href="/eb5-investment-process">EB-5 investment process</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>For students</h2>
  <p>
    Vietnamese F-1 students may weigh EB-5 against the traditional OPT → H-1B → employment-based green card sequence.
    EB-5 does not automatically convert F-1 status; it is a separate petition. Earlier planning during school can help
    with gift documentation and project diligence before work-authorization windows narrow. Shared student framing is on
    <a href="/pathways/f1-to-eb5-self-sponsored-green-card">F-1 to EB-5 self-sponsored green card</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>For families funding an investment</h2>
  <p>
    Parental gifts are common when a child is the investor of record. USCIS requires a complete trail from the original
    lawful source through the gift and into the investment enterprise. Cross-border remittance and tax rules should be
    reviewed with advisers familiar with both Vietnamese and U.S. requirements before capital moves. More on lawful
    funding structures:
    <a href="/research/ways-to-fund-eb5-investment-2026">ways to fund an EB-5 investment</a>.
  </p>
</PathwayLandingLayout>
